// A rest binding of a nominal record is that record's remainder, closed BY
// its declaration. `P` and `Q` share a shape and are different types, so a
// remainder of `Q` is never a `P`. It was: the TName arm re-bound a row that
// was already closed, and passing the rest to `f` checked clean and ran.
type P = {a: Int, b: Int}
type Q = {a: Int, b: Int}

fn f(p: P) = p.a

fn main() = match (Q{a: 1, b: 2}) {
  {...rest} => f(rest),
}
